      "content": "so you get it. it's like being forced to watch a slow-motion car crash every single day. it's exhausting and it's just... heavy. i don't want to be the one left holding the ashes when it's all finally gone. is there any dignity in just leaving before the end becomes even more ugly? like, is there honor in not being there to see the total wreckage?",
